This is quite nonsensical. You don't seem to have understood the
strategy. I read the scroll of earth long before I meet Demogorgon. It
does not cost a move during the confrontation.

So here is the strategy description again, to make everything clear.
When I notice that I am on D's level, I read an uncursed scroll of earth
on the staircase. I move out of the boulder fort and push the moved
boulder back (I described that before, but you seem to have forgotten
it). I have already read a scroll of magic mapping after detecting that
this is D's level. I proceed to a place behind a wall but that will be
in his line of sight, once the wall is gone. I engrave Elbereth. I dig a
hole in the wall. D appears and turns to flee. I hit him until he
teleports away (next to the stairs but not on them, because they are
blocked by a boulder; in vanilla I would instead have put some item and
engraved Elbereth on the stairs, so he cannot be on them). I quaff a
cursed potion of gain level and go to the downstairs. When I go down, I
am in my boulder fort (in slash'em) or on an Elbereth square (in
vanilla). In slash'em, I shoot him, without his ever being able to touch
me, in vanilla I beat him to death.

It was not me who suggested writing Elbereth only after coming down the
stairs again.  I would write it on the first descent, not on the second,
if I chose a melee approach (and I would not use a boulder at all in
that case, any other item would do; boulders are only useful here, if
you make a fort). In my original description, the purpose of the scroll
of earth was to prevent D from getting to the stairs. That purpose would
not be served, if you read the scroll only when getting down the
staircase the second time. You might land next to the stairs and D could
be on them.

Both methods are pretty safe, the advantage of the slash'em method is
that if D could summon monsters that don't respect Elbereth (which I do
not know; he can summon some, and as far as I remember, that was not
restricted to demons, but I may be wrong here), I would not have to (and
don't) care. So depending on D's summoning capabilities, my slash'em
method is slightly safer (but it is not available in vanilla due to the
lack of great missile weapons, so there I would proceed differently, if
I wanted to meet D at all, and I would choose the Orcus level to get him).




